      "writtenOn": "2026-07-29T09:16:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "question: just so that I understand ACL properly, here this line means:\n```\nusers have rw rights\nuser 424242 has rw rights\ngroups have r rights\ngroup 434343 has rx rights\n? have rwx rights\nothers has no rights\n```\n\nAm i correct ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 23,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 23,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "b2fa724acc8755709cb4942acb8a1a9e58c65f24",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f1d0e724_829f8bec",
        "filename": "rbh-sync/tests/acl/test_acl_db_sync.bash",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 23,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039469
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-29T09:30:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not for all:\n\n`u::rw-` means that the owning user have `rw` rights\n\n`g::r--` means that the owning group have `r` rights\n\n`m::rwx` means that the maximum effective permissions for named users and the group class are `rwx`",
      "parentUuid": "8148b880_13783496",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 23,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 23,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "b2fa724acc8755709cb4942acb8a1a9e58c65f24",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
